{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLp5STui5xf6LPLLZgb6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `Pow.as_real_imag` in `sympy/core/power.py`. It used to return `(self, 0)` whenever the base had no imaginary part, even when the exponent was negative and the base might be zero. In that case the expression could really be `zoo`, whose parts are `nan`, so `(self, 0)` was wrong. Now, for a negative integer exponent where the base isn't known to be nonzero, it returns `(re(self), im(self))` and leaves them unevaluated.\n\nResults after the change:\n- `Pow(Sum(1, (p, 8, 6)), -1).as_real_imag()` gives `(re(1/Sum(...)), im(1/Sum(...)))`, where it used to give `(1/Sum(...), 0)`.\n- `Pow(0, -1).as_real_imag()` is still `(nan, nan)`.\n- When the base is known to be nonzero, nothing changes: for a positive `y`, `(1/y).as_real_imag()` is still `(1/y, 0)`.\n\nOne behaviour change you should know about: for a real symbol `x` with no other assumptions, `(1/x).as_real_imag()` now gives `(re(1/x), im(1/x))` instead of `(1/x, 0)`. That's because `x` could be zero, so this is the same fix applied to a common case. Any code that relied on getting `(1/x, 0)` back will see the unevaluated form.\n\nThe tests in `sympy/core`, `sympy/functions/elementary`, `sympy/functions/special`, `sympy/concrete` and `sympy/simplify` all pass. I didn't run the rest of the suite.\n\nThe new check only covers bases with no imaginary part. A complex base that could be zero, with a negative exponent, still goes down the old path, which divides by `re**2 + im**2`. I left that alone to keep the change small."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":302,"cache_read_input_tokens":23655,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":302},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14725469-559d-462d-a519-9f833d3b9be8","uuid":"c580c4c6-3507-4622-8340-6ff35a6812e1","timestamp":"2026-11-24T00:33:05.373Z","request_id":"req_011ChLp5SKyrGettntxE9pFH"}
